--- /dev/null
+++ b/DIAGNOSTIC-TESTING.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+Atria 1.9.3+qwellldiag1 / RootHide diagnostic / GPL-3.0-or-later
+Base: CySxL/Atria 97487ef45c7bbd335f5f69d7a5568dbf44175ec7.
+This replaces com.cysxl.atria (same package identifier); never install as a second Atria.
+No qwelllfix1 scale behavior changes. GridLayout short casts are build compatibility only.
+Remove/disable AtriaZoomGuard and any older independent scaling patch before testing.
+The package conflicts with com.qwelll.atriazoomguard. Preserve existing Atria settings.
+Install the deb with the RootHide package manager, then respring using your normal tool.
+No device result or fix success is claimed. This is temporary diagnostics, not a fix.
+
+Test on iOS 17.2.1:
+1. Set a clearly non-default Home Screen icon scale; note the value externally.
+2. Wait 5 seconds after SpringBoard reload so startup logs have flushed.
+3. Open an app from the Home Screen, remain there 3 seconds, return Home normally.
+4. Repeat 2-3 times; avoid scrolling/wiggle/edit mode during each capture.
+5. Repeat with an app in Dock and non-default Dock scale as the control case.
+6. Wait at least 5 seconds after the last return; collect log and .1 if present.
+7. Optional iOS 15 control, same settings. Record OS, scale settings, test times,
+   gesture/button exit and observed flash externally, without identifying apps.
+8. Restore a regular Atria build after collecting logs to remove diagnostic overhead.
+
+Log priority: SpringBoard's own NSHomeDirectory()/Documents/AtriaReturnDiagnostic.log
+Typical non-container home: /var/mobile/Documents/AtriaReturnDiagnostic.log
+Fallback: /tmp/AtriaReturnDiagnostic.log (sometimes /private/var/tmp equivalent).
+RootHide virtual paths and SpringBoard home can differ. Check from the SpringBoard
+jailbreak environment, not merely the terminal app's own sandbox home.
+Use a privileged file manager to check these paths and their .1 rotated siblings.
+LOAD qwellldiag1 marker includes OS, method encodings and enabled/skipped hook checks.
+Absence of a file alone does NOT prove failure to load: check paths, write permissions,
+RootHide injection enablement, selected app/process and package version separately.
+Logs never include app names, bundle IDs, UI text, images or object addresses.
+viewID is an incrementing opaque view-object ID reset on SpringBoard restart;
+view reuse means it is NOT an app identifier. superclass is the superview class.
+t is seconds since 2001-01-01 UTC; uptime is monotonic seconds.
+Matrices are m11,m12,...,m44. Null presentation means no available presentation layer.
+seq preserves accepted observation order. before / afterOrig / afterAtria distinguish
+system method and the unchanged upstream Atria scaling operation.
+
+Only SBApplicationIcon in explicit Home/Dock enum locations is sampled.
+Skipped: folders/widgets/App Library and off-main-thread calls. No arbitrary subtree
+walks: only contentContainerView and existing _iconImageView object ivar are read.
+No global UIView/CALayer hooks, no scale/animation/layout/visibility setters added.
+_applyIconContentScale:, _updateIconContentScale verified against iOS17 header:
+MTACS/iOS-17-Runtime-Headers PrivateFrameworks/SpringBoardHome.framework/SBIconView.h
+blob 6f32dbd5ec067750c2bb79d5503d7fd0251c0d3f.
+All three optional hooks (including inherited setHidden:) require matching runtime
+return/argument encodings. Missing/mismatched methods are skipped, never invented.
+Effective/normal scale getters have a reentrancy guard; nested diagnostic reads skip.
+
+Performance limits: 480 records in the overwrite buffer, at most one 480-record
+in-flight batch (960 total queued observations). 2-second event-driven merge;
+no periodic sampling, no periodic scale refresh, JSON/file work on serial I/O queue.
+Slow I/O cannot enqueue unlimited batches. Overwrites emit ring_overwrite count.
+Log rotates at >2 MiB before append to one .1 backup (each can exceed by one batch).
+This bounds memory and disk, not zero timing impact: private getters and presentation
+reads can perturb timing. Reproduce without diagnostics as a control.
